A1. The kind of honker Dr. Seuss would use on his car. ~ GANDER
A6. These take the girls. ~ ESCORTS
A13. An attack by the drys. ~ RAID
A14. Get. ~ SECURE
A15. Just grass. ~ HERBAGE
A18. When your favorite horse comes in. ~ LATE
A19. Thusly. ~ SO
A20. Who made Uncle Tom tearful? ~ EVA
A21. For fear that. ~ LEST
A23. French article. ~ LE
A24. A word that generally starts arguments. ~ BUT
A25. You can raise this with the jack. ~ RENT
A27. Anyone can lick this. ~ STAMP
A29. Saucy, so to speak. ~ PERT
A30. Impels. ~ URGES
A32. An oversize monkey. ~ APE
A33. A sure way to get a puzzle. ~ SOLVE
A34. How an architect puts up. ~ ERECTS
A36. There. ~ AT
A37. Forcibly taken. ~ LED
A39. According to a song this "Ain't what it used to be." ~ MARE
A40. Enough to make any man fall. ~ GIRL
A42. Helen Wills takes this easily. ~ SET
A44. A personal pronoun. ~ MY
A45. Stay. ~ REMAIN
A48. People are always acting up in these. ~ PLAYS
A50. This is a joke. ~ PUN
A51. There's little of this below the Rio Grande. ~ PEACE
A53. Matrimonial confetti. ~ RICE
A54. What do you put up for robbers? ~ HANDS
A56. Out of. ~ FROM
A57. What insect razzed the grasshopper? ~ ANT
