D2. To put in order. ~ ARRANGE
D3. Grab. ~ NAB
D4. Turn this and get your station. ~ DIAL
D5. These are found on the border. ~ EDGES
D6. Slippery fish! ~ EEL
D7. An Indian trophy. ~ SCALP
D8. What your baby always is. ~ CUTE
D9. Unrefined iron—that's hard! ~ ORE
D10. A football position. (abbr.) ~ RE
D11. No matter where leopards hide they're always this. ~ SPOTTED
D12. This is a beautiful child. ~ CHERUB
D16. Always. ~ EVER
D17. What heirs often quarrel over. ~ ESTATE
D19. Look over. ~ SURVEY
